  "notes": "Closed-score SATB: Soprano+Alto share the treble staff, Tenor+Bass share the bass staff. A correct conversion yields FOUR parts (Soprano, Alto, Tenor, Bass), each with its own notes; all three verses belong to the Soprano part (lyric numbers 1-3) and must stay attached to soprano notes, including melisma skips (e.g. \"pre - cious\" spans a slurred melisma). DAMAGE (crop): Image edges cut through the staves. Mild: tight crop 0.4 mm outside the staff ends (braces/brackets cut off), header kept. Scan: header (title/credits) cropped away, 0.8 mm cut into the staff starts and 3.0 mm off the staff ends (end barlines gone). Severe: cut 1.24 mm into the staff starts (up to just before the first clef / part name / lyric) and 6.83 mm off the ends (to just after the right-most notehead/stem/lyric). Cut amounts are computed per page from the clean raster so that no clef, key/time signature, notehead, stem, accidental, lyric or part name is removed - only staff-line ends, brackets/braces, barlines and the header. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Barlines at system starts/ends (incl. the final barline) are partly or completely cut off - they are still present in the truth. scan/severe: title/composer/poet header text is not visible; ignore work-title/creators when scoring."
